/-!
# Shared word data for Fi23 centralizer exhaustion

Breadth-first search from zero-based letter 15181 through the literal left
ATLAS generators supplies a word for each of 31671 labels. A sentinel 1
encodes the empty word; appending generator A or B changes code c to 2c or
2c+1. Thus the least-significant digits give the product word in Lean order.
The maximum word length is 46. These data alone assert no exhaustion theorem.

Reproduce with `Exhaustion/source/generate.py --check`; the original ATLAS
files and attribution are retained in `AtlasCarriers/source/`. The application
is GLS3 Table 5.3u and its conjugation description. Each computation used as
mathematics must be checked separately in Lean.
-/

@[expose] public section
